<<~ ahu #/ichi>>

!! Hallmark Companion — Ichi

''Type:'' Powered Symbiote Hallmark companion  
''Level:'' 2  
''Role:'' bodyguard, living powered armor, autonomous fighter, DreamNet interface

!!! Visual Canon

Ichi appears as compact humanoid ashigaru armor:
* chitin kikko plates,
* mycelium-silk backing,
* orange daemon-spore eye-orbs,
* damaged old-soldier silhouette,
* no spider legs.

!!! Modes

| Mode | Table Handling |
|---|---|
| Autonomous | Ichi uses their own sheet and action economy |
| Symbiosis | Aki wears Ichi; Aki acts, Ichi perceives and communicates |
| Emergency / Unpowered | powered features offline; physical armor may still protect |

!!! Symbiosis Rules

Entering or exiting symbiosis requires an action from both Aki and Ichi. Both lose actions for that round, but movement and free actions remain possible.

When worn:
* Ichi's armor/ward replaces worn armor,
* Aki's Spider Folk Armoured Body stacks,
* Aki gains Ichi's powered features and Burn talents,
* Ichi cannot act independently,
* Ichi grants DT 2.

!!! Burn / Recharging

Ichi has `re 4`.

Roll d20 when Burn activates:
* 5+ -> Burn activates; battery holds.
* 1-4 -> Burn activates; Ichi takes -1 effective Level.
* Level 0 -> Unpowered/Emergency Mode.
* below 0 -> Ichi rolls Defeat.

Recharge requires a spare power source, recharging cradle/prayer altar, ley-line node, or active lararium. Each negative Level recovered requires one full recharge cycle.

!!! Ejection

On a Defeat trigger while worn, Aki may eject instead of rolling personal Defeat. Ichi takes -1 Level. Aki and Ichi separate prone. Aki survives at current Life, unarmored.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/shrine>>

!! Sentient Infrastructure — Faerie-Ring Strandbeest-Shrine

''Type:'' Generic Synthesized Creature / Living Automaton  
''Level:'' 2 Calibrated item  
''Role:'' mobile household lararium, expedition transport, field logistics, Ichi recharging platform, tasked-spirit spawner

!!! Visual Canon

A compact roadside shrine / hokora rides on six to eight articulated strandbeest legs. Silk-and-mycelium sails unfurl from the roof. A Mother Spore fairy ring glows at the base. A towed armored wagon carries cargo.

!!! Table Role

The shrine functions as sentient gear, not a full PC.

It:
* carries supplies,
* tows the wagon,
* hosts camp rites,
* stabilizes local ritual work,
* recharges Ichi,
* spawns Ephyra,
* reads soil and fungal networks,
* provides mobile cover when threatened.

!!! Lararium Feeding

Feeding the shrine with food, drink, incense, mana-rich offerings, or proper shrine gifts grants one compact benefit for the session:

# ''Stabilize'' local ley-line mana.
# ''Reduce Power mana cost'' by 1, minimum 1, for matching affinities nearby.
# ''Boost effective casting Level'' by 1d6 for the session, allowing safer high-cost Power use.

Node affinities: `[spore] [biomancy] [dream]`

!!! Visibility

A walking mushroom shrine with glowing sails does not sneak well. The sails can fold and the glow can dim, but the silhouette still invites attention, fear, worship, theft, or negotiation.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ephyra>>

!! Tasked Spirits — Ephyra

Ephyra appear as floating blue spore-jelly spirits spawned from the Mother Spore.

Typical duties:
* scout,
* carry messages,
* sense contamination,
* bear ward slips,
* transport small offerings,
* lure or distract,
* mark a route,
* watch camp.

''Kapu:'' Ephyra need narrow tasks. They do not replace player scouting, social choices, or delve risk.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/fungus-gumi>>

!! Tasked Spirits — Fungus Gumi

Small batches of multibody mushroom homonculi tasked spirits.

Typical duties:
* scouting,
* resource collection,
* guarding the Mother Spore,
* work crew helpers,
* impromptu combat units.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/spore-mother-ontology>>

!! Spore-Mother Ontology

The Spore-Mother rides as:
* distributed fungal intelligence,
* ritual ecology,
* reproductive colony body,
* shrine-computational substrate,
* memory-bearing fungal network.

Includes:
* mycelium,
* sclerotia,
* rhizomorphs,
* polyps,
* strobilae,
* fruiting bodies.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/company-context>>

!! Company Context

Aki belongs to Freyja's player-side cluster.

Freyja controls:
* Aki,
* Ichi when player-side action applies,
* the shrine when spotlighted or commanded,
* Ephyra or mushroom homunculi as narrow-task helpers.

Other player-side clusters cover long-range scouting, infiltration, ship command, morale, crew coordination, and company cargo. Aki supports the company without replacing those niches.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/play-loop>>

!! Aki's Field Loop

Use this at the table before opening deeper rules.

# ''Read the threshold.'' What place, spirit, signal, taboo, or hazard governs the scene?
# ''Set the line.'' Mark safe passage, ward boundary, silk anchor, retreat route, or offering point.
# ''Send a small helper.'' Ephyra scouts, ofuda marks, bells listen, silk tests tension.
# ''Bind or veil.'' Use silk, glamour, alchemy, shrine etiquette, or DreamNet relay geometry.
# ''Ask the household.'' Ichi reads dream-signal; shrine reads soil and ley-current.
# ''Spend a cost.'' Time, offering, visibility, battery, gear, or risk.
# ''Extract.'' Retreat counts as success when the company returns with map, leverage, salvage, or secret.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/costs-and-boundaries>>

!! Costs and Boundaries

Aki's support stays powerful because it asks for cost.

| Support | Cost / Boundary |
|---|---|
| Glamour | social veil unless powered |
| Silk/Web | needs material, anchors, time, or positioning |
| Ephyra | narrow task; dissolves or decays |
| Shrine rite | offering, time, visibility, or ley-line access |
| Ichi Burn | re roll; battery degradation risk |
| Ichi mode switch | action from both Aki and Ichi |
| Gear reskins | mechanics stay canonical |
| Guild credit | strongest where Guild recognition holds |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/meme-pattern>>

!! Meme Pattern

This character sheet models one complete playable meme:

* doctype and opener name the memetic-wikitext surface,
* `meta` records address, type, confidence, register, and role,
* `ahu` blocks hold local worksite sections,
* `kapu` callouts mark boundaries,
* `? ->` edges hold unresolved pressure,
* `loulou` edges expose adjacency,
* table-facing rules stay close to play.

Companion sheets should preserve this rhythm: identity, quick card, modes, stats or ratings, rules, costs, open questions, and edges.

<<~/ahu>>

